s, between 1 and 4. Each lost customer removes £300 a month of monthly recurring revenue. The starter tier would win about 150 new subscribers, between 80 and 250. Each starter subscriber adds £49 a month to monthly recurring revenue. Each starter subscriber costs about £6 a month in support. Keeping pricing as it is adds nothing.","assistant_message":"I’ve built the comparison around your three pricing choices and your target of at least **£126,000 monthly recurring revenue** within nine months. Carrying on as now holds today’s values.\n\nA provisional first pass ran on Olumi’s drafted links, but none of it is confirmed, so it is something to challenge rather than an answer. The key unresolved mechanism is how starter-tier price and subscriber numbers combine into starter-tier MRR.\n\nI’ve read your goal, ‘monthly recurring revenue’, as the total across every tier, including ‘Starter-tier MRR’. If you meant only part of it, say which.\n\nThe model was saved."},{"turn_id":"8a32f08a-773e-486c-90fc-007356b39025","created_at":"2026-10-07T04:45:25.563941+00:00","user_message":"Run analysis","assistant_message":"Your results are ready. You can view them now or ask me to explain them."},{"turn_id":"9b3edfdf-c8ab-4854-80f7-72f3efa1f5ca","created_at":"2026-10-07T04:45:39.959859+00:00","user_message":"Explain this result","assistant_message":"No single option can be put forward: the options do not clearly separate, and small changes can alter the comparison. This result also rests on eight values supplied by Olumi, not you.\n\n‘monthly recurring revenue’ was checked against the figures in your model. For ‘Raise Prices 10%’ and ‘Launch Starter Tier’ it couldn’t be checked: those options move it through a link Olumi hasn’t sized in this limit’s units.\n\nHow much do ‘Existing-price rise’ and ‘Starter-tier availability’ each change ‘monthly recurring revenue’?","suggested_actions":[{"id":"agent-next-pre-mortem","label":"Run a pre-mortem","message":"Run a pre-mortem with me: ima